{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Sampling Rate.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Sampling Rate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sensor sampling rate sensor sampling rate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Sampling Rate.md","fileName":"Sensor Sampling Rate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sensor Sampling Rate","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-10-04 23:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Self-Tracking Markets and Institutional Power]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Self-Tracking Markets and Institutional Power","self-tracking.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Sampling Rate.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Sampling Rate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sensor sampling rate sensor sampling rate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sensor Sampling Rate.md","fileName":"Sensor Sampling Rate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sensor Sampling Rate","heading":"Sensor Sampling Rate","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Sensor sampling rate is the frequency at which a sensing system takes measurements. A higher rate can preserve faster changes and finer timing, while a lower rate produces fewer observations and may miss short events.\n\nThe appropriate rate depends on the phenomenon and question. Slowly changing daily activity may tolerate widely spaced samples, whereas a rapidly changing physiological signal may require much denser measurement. More samples also increase storage, battery, transmission, and analysis demands.\n\nSampling rate is part of the context needed to interpret self-tracking data. A smooth summary can hide gaps or processing, so a meaningful export should distinguish the original sampling schedule from later aggregation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Self-Tracking Markets and Institutional Power",